<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ceuta: EU grants Spain €115 million in emergency aid</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f256316f3472150e2cbdadd127845e24962fa12f4a70737305bfeb3fd833dd9</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ceuta-eu-grants-spain-_115-million-in-emergency-aid/a-79206505--754cf3a038a5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ceuta-eu-grants-spain-€115-million-in-emergency-aid/a-79206505?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU has said the funds will go toward bolstering border security and returning migrants to Morocco. The move comes in the wake of a crisis that saw more than 70,000 migrants overwhelm the Spanish exclave in July.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the September 11, 2001 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:906dced0787da2a940588a14eb9fcf77743e955b056e97359a763defb3bf4902</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T17:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918--22a07e00351f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-september-11-2001-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 attacks were partly planned in Hamburg, via the so-called Hamburg cell, whose members played key roles in the plot. A look back at a day that shook up Germany’s approach to national security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e658c79a180d1f124012533e7d8cbd09668bfbe19fb3257f41ad2cc0dea54ae</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Switzerland: Two killed in power plant explosion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:336e598cb7fc37c48d685d1bc0697d43d91d6955c20db08e08e633766aa4dcdb</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/switzerland-two-killed-in-power-plant-explosion/a-79205516--3f73e13d5b04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/switzerland-two-killed-in-power-plant-explosion/a-79205516?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fire and subsequent explosion have killed two workers at a Swiss hydroelectric power plant. Authorities say the facility suffered major damage in the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran tightens social control with crackdown on cafes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7bb1b2d391a9f564441785990bcd16cddc62f98965f83ce94e00667be198171</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988--56f8af8e2572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-tightens-social-control-with-crackdown-on-cafes/a-79204988?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities are keeping a close eye on cafes, fearing they could play a role in fostering anti-government sentiment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's constitutional reform: What does it mean — especially for Abiy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b525a7d7a72116c6cb9ff072363dc6dc7d9735dc97ab3d0121818e0c6a36086</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262--7aa1de37183a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-constitutional-reform-what-does-it-mean-especially-for-abiy/a-79172262?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed stands to benefit from a planned constitutional reform in the country. A new presidential system would reshape political power — and could give him a more powerful mandate in office.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Oil prices rise as Middle East conflict escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16af4d630f22d16ffb8411efd84bb673c9d291bc7f527e14bb000eb5455d9e01</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T14:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oil-prices-rise-as-middle-east-conflict-escalates/a-79203547--69f3e58c677b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oil-prices-rise-as-middle-east-conflict-escalates/a-79203547?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The price of oil returned to triple digits in US dollars, as conflict in the Middle East threatens supply chains and puts a strain on global reserves.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Syria arms depot explosion kills at least 14</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2690309a801d6ff1bdc39ef073e2ef86eb28b89e63ddcdf1e49e01c0739b62c6</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314--22d7b8669d08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-arms-depot-explosion-kills-at-least-14/a-79203314?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The explosion struck near the Syrian city of Sarmada in Idlib province in the northwest. The Defense Ministry said the weapons and remnants from the war were being stored temporarily at the site before being relocated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6e0c973e45c2afd8b9b36e42f8e51dcebfd1f66ef5f5421e7b25cc67a40a9ff</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285--d234556fa838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The documentary "Letters From the Silenced Country" depicts the ongoing repression under the authoritarian regime. Director Andrei Kutsila talked to DW ahead of the film's Venice premiere.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why we're still looking for dark matter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:459d46454443e1b478a5788463e4c71f3cad7b105af147c85930251bbc02119d</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:21:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395--3bfbe0fa2ce3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When physicists said they may have spotted evidence of dark matter almost 100 years after it was proposed as a theory, the internet lit up. Here's why we're searching for the thing that holds everything else together.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Cambodia's floating schools hit by rising fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49587ae4dbc78cfdc15d0968c8d08ad9e75fd94e5414ba57a6b3d3aa1a5bced7</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008--dc2e9aeeea22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran war has sent fuel prices higher in Cambodia, squeezing families who rely on fishing and boats for their livelihoods. For children living on Tonle Sap, rising fuel costs pose yet another barrier to education.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU proposes more restrictions for Airbnb, holiday rentals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bec79878793ea3e7a9bd0a2623226a170f32baf1dfff93a680ac3e81e9f13d87</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-more-restrictions-for-airbnb-holiday-rentals/a-79202023--ad637f480100.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-proposes-more-restrictions-for-airbnb-holiday-rentals/a-79202023?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants tighter rules on short-term rentals to tackle housing shortages in tourist hotspots.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: How  the 'house of sisters' threat split society</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bedb9c01b8fa0445e336327b93d793bf9d7a65b8218db2efffe0d03966402170</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163--b9de2b546f7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/syria-how-the-house-of-sisters-threat-split-society/a-79192163?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rumor has it that the 'house of sisters' is where kidnapped women from other Syrian sects are forced to convert to Islam. Nobody knows if it really exists, but it's being used to create communal tensions anyway.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>LIV Golf in financial turmoil: what's next for the sport?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b5b8e10e4e80a556aac1c28d71bc005c6565cf300a6ffa56f3ea6ff2fb648eb</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569--378367d5fd0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Six months after Saudi Arabia pulled funding from the breakaway organization, LIV Golf have filed for bankruptcy protection. Several of the world's best players signed on to LIV, so where does that leave golf?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's King Harald V laid to rest in state funeral</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87f2501b2c00113b2e600051b6977eeeb79ba549ccce541a8bf8f1d80395682d</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-v-laid-to-rest-in-state-funeral/a-79199812--18dfde6e8405.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-king-harald-v-laid-to-rest-in-state-funeral/a-79199812?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Heads of state from around the world came to Oslo to pay tribute to the late monarch.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia dissolves parliament as snap elections called</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:344221875c6d6340f0d0f6126037304af3f6e9efa4b77874377bf98ddd5af8fc</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-dissolves-parliament-as-snap-elections-called/a-79200868--9098381ff4d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-dissolves-parliament-as-snap-elections-called/a-79200868?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Serbia will head to the polls in late October after President Aleksandar Vucic dissolved parliament following growing pressure from protesters demanding political change. However, Vucic plans to stand as a PM candidate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Conspiracy theories can provide answers but not peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6233c2f6f0447c8f3f095fbc7581d41ee7a608438ee2decb3489b1c3b2643a1a</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756--b464ce7f771c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Twenty-five years after 9/11, conspiracy theories about the terrorist attacks persist. But even as an attempt to make sense of a tragedy, psychologists say the benefit in conspiracy ideation or belief is short-lived.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>UK rules out cyberattack after major flight disruptions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45569c963176d08d42ba4683e457dbf7755c7d1221d76096b584fb572dd5176f</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-rules-out-cyberattack-after-major-flight-disruptions/a-79197818--dd3ac7957051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-rules-out-cyberattack-after-major-flight-disruptions/a-79197818?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Airports across the UK continue to face delays and cancellations after a flight processing system failure. The UK's transport secretary has summoned the CEO of National Air Traffic Services (NATS) for an explanation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfaa97800c4f6f1cab607acfe1d8998e70754a655815ac2adb31aab76e4c5410</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>India: 5 baby orangutans rescued, smuggling suspected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f9c234dff6bbacbedff041c7127be0510fd1febb15961d5e1e7e5d3d1f2477f</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-5-baby-orangutans-rescued-smuggling-suspected/live-79195914--34bc38c447a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-5-baby-orangutans-rescued-smuggling-suspected/live-79195914?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five young orangutans, not native to India, were found in an Odisha forest, sparking suspicion of an international smuggling operation. Meanwhile, India said it was not involved in the BAPS-Eiffel Tower row.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5ce8c32079c136ba57da331b5d1f7584e1672fb39c748c3ad92f9d026f1a4d9</id><updated>2026-09-09T19:20:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cambodia's crackdown on scam operators is stranding young African trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
